    "body": "Global logistics provider DSV has opened a new $90 million, 853,000-square-foot logistics facility in Laredo, Texas, expanding its capacity to handle freight moving between the U.S. and Mexico .\nThe facility consolidates warehousing, transportation, customs brokerage, inventory management and distribution services under one roof, the company announced Wednesday.\nThe investment is part of DSV’s broader strategy to strengthen its North American cross-border logistics network , which also includes a recently opened office in McAllen, Texas .\n“Our Laredo facility is a milestone in DSV’s strategy to lead with innovation and scale,” Josh Summers, CEO of Contract Logistics, North America, said in a news release . “We’re committed to helping our customers grow by providing smarter, more agile logistics solutions.”\nThe new multi-client complex is located along Interstate 35 in Laredo, one of the nation’s busiest gateways for commercial trade with Mexico.\nAccording to FreightWaves SONAR, shippers currently hold solid negotiating leverage with carriers in Laredo. As of Oct. 21, the Outbound Tender Rejection Index (STRI) has dropped from 8.15% a month ago to 5.10%\nIn Laredo, Texas, carriers are facing a loosening environment with outbound tender rejections (STRI.LRD) falling to 5.10%, giving shippers the upper hand. To learn more about FreightWaves SONAR, click here .\nDSV broke ground on the new project in Laredo in July 2025 at a 49-acre site within Majestic Realty’s Port Grande Logistics Park, a 2,000-acre industrial development.\nThe facility supports a range of logistics operations, including cross-docking, e-commerce fulfillment, inventory management, distribution and cross-border transportation.\nIt also offers bonded warehousing and Foreign-Trade Zone storage options, along with northbound U.S. customs services and on-site Mexican customs processing.\nThose capabilities are designed to help shippers reduce delays, streamline customs clearance and improve freight visibility when moving goods between the two countries.\nThe facilities in Laredo and McAllen complement DSV’s existing border operations in Brownsville, El Paso and Los Indios, Texas, as well as San Diego, California.\nThe Laredo operation is part of DSV’s global logistics network, which employs approximately 150,000 people in more than 90 countries.\nWhy it matters: DSV’s investments in Laredo and McAllen, Texas, adds integrated freight handling and customs capabilities at one of North America’s busiest trade gateways.\nUpcoming FreightWaves Events\nCompliance\nBrokerage Compliance Symposium\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nAwards\nF3 Awards Dinner\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nFreightTech\nF3: Future of Freight Festival\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nOctober 27, 2026 – October 28, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nCompliance Brokerage Compliance Symposium Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nAwards F3 Awards Dinner Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nFreightTech F3: Future of Freight Festival Oct 27 – Oct 28 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now",
